# Mapstack — Agent Guide

## Overview
A minimalist, mobile-first mapping web app with multi-layer GeoJSON, GPX, and Komoot Tour link import support.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework:** React 18 + TypeScript + Vite
- **Mapping:** Leaflet + React-Leaflet
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` (standardized to `18px`, `strokeWidth={2}`)
- **Styling:** Pure custom CSS (`src/index.css`) — no Tailwind or external UI component libraries.
- **Server / API:** Node HTTP middleware registered in `vite.config.ts` for development/preview, with a serverless adapter in `api/`.
- **Testing:** Node's built-in `node:test` runner with Vite `ssrLoadModule` for TypeScript modules; no separate test framework.
- **SSL / Mobile Dev:** `@vitejs/plugin-basic-ssl` providing HTTPS for mobile geolocation testing.

## Design Principles
- **Typography:** Google Font `Inconsolata` for all typography (body, inputs, buttons, popups, and dialogs).
  - Minimum text size: **16px (1em)** (`--font-size-base`) across all UI elements, inputs, and buttons to avoid mobile iOS Safari auto-zoom on input focus.
  - Secondary size: **18px** (`--font-size-md`) for headers and popup titles.
- **Color Palette:** Minimalist greyscale foundation + single interactive accent color (`#ff4d00` / `var(--accent)`).
- **Icons:** Normalized to `18px` with `strokeWidth={2}` across controls, buttons, dialogs, and cards. Use `currentColor` / greyscale for neutral actions, white on solid accent buttons.
- **Buttons:**
  - Primary: `.btn-primary` (solid accent fill, white text).
  - Secondary: `.btn-secondary` (accent stroke and text, transparent fill, light accent hover tint). Used for the file chooser and add stop.
  - Toggle choices: `.profile-btn` with `.active` for the selected option. Inactive choices use accent stroke/text; the active choice uses a solid accent fill with white text. Shared by travel modes and import source choices.
- **Control Height:** All inputs and buttons share `--control-height: 44px` so inline controls align vertically (`.search-input`, `.btn`, `.btn-sm`, `.btn-icon`, `.btn-icon-only`, `.wp-locate-btn`, `.profile-btn`). Map zoom and locate buttons (`.zoom-btn`, `.locate-btn`) are exactly `44px × 44px`.
- **No Emoji in UI:** Use `lucide-react` icons rather than emoji glyphs in new UI text/labels.
- **Layout & Viewport:** Mobile-first, full-bleed map (`100vw` x `100dvh` with `-webkit-fill-available` fallback):
  - **Screen Margin:** Standardized `--screen-margin: 16px` from viewport edges.
  - **Top-right:** Custom Lucide icon zoom controls and the floating locate button (`.locate-btn`) grouped in `.map-floating-controls`; every button is `44px × 44px`, with `--panel-radius: 20px` and neutral monochrome styling.
  - **Bottom Dock:** Fixed `.bottom-dock` (`position: fixed`) floating above mobile browser toolbars with `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` offsets containing:
    1. Horizontal standalone layer cards stack (`.layer-card-stack`) floating directly above the controls, with the newest layer first (leftmost). The scroll viewport is full-bleed with `16px` internal start/end spacing so partially visible cards clip at the physical screen edges. Cards have explicit `min(80vw, 320px)` width limits and a `92px` height. Content is top-aligned, visibility/delete icons stack vertically, and titles wrap to a maximum of three lines with an ellipsis. Activating a partially visible card smooth-scrolls it fully into view and marks it active with an accent border / `aria-current`. Tap the active title to edit; the editing textarea and card expand to show the full name. Edits commit on blur, Enter confirms, and Escape cancels. The stack uses native horizontal overflow scrolling without scroll snapping.
    2. 3-button action pill (`.bottom-action-bar`): `[Search]`, `[New Route]`, `[Import]`.
  - **Action & Modal Naming:** Each dialog title exactly matches its bottom-bar action: `Search`, `New Route`, and `Import`.
  - **Layer Cards:** Squarer corners (`--card-radius: 6px`) to distinguish from rounded control pills.
  - **Input Panels / Modals:** Top-docked on mobile (`align-items: flex-start; padding-top: calc(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px) + var(--screen-margin))`) to avoid virtual keyboard occlusion, centered dialogs on desktop (`min-width: 640px`). Transparent blur-only backdrop (`backdrop-filter: blur(8px)`), elevated shadow (`--shadow-input-panel`), and touch overscroll containment.

## Accessibility (A11y) Standards
- **Form Controls:** Every input must be programmatically associated with a label via `htmlFor` / `id` or an explicit `aria-label` (route stop inputs use `aria-label` since their visible labels were removed for full-width layout).
- **Dialogs:** All modals use `ModalDialog.tsx` with `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `aria-labelledby`, focus trapping, focus restoration, and Escape key dismissal.
- **Accessible Names:** All icon-only buttons must provide explicit `aria-label` attributes.
- **Keyboard Navigation:** Autocomplete suggestions use `<button role="option">` inside `<ul role="listbox">`. Layer cards are labelled groups with `aria-current` on the active route; native title buttons handle activation/editing, and all action buttons remain keyboard accessible.
- **Focus Indicators:** Global `:focus-visible` outline (`2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px`).
- **Text Selection:** `user-select: none` is restricted only to draggable map controls and toolbars, leaving body text selectable.

## Map, Layer & Geolocation Rules
- **Color Allocation:** Layers automatically cycle through distinct high-contrast colors via `LAYER_PALETTE` in `src/hooks/useMapLayers.ts`.
- **Card & Marker Sync:** Route path, waypoint pin markers, and layer card indicator dots synchronously share the layer's allocated color.
- **Waypoints:** Classified from GPX metadata into Lucide teardrop pin markers (`Tent`, `Utensils`, `Beer`, `Bed`, `Castle`, etc.) with interactive popups displaying name and notes.
- **User Location:** Live GPS tracked via `useUserLocation.ts`. Displayed as a **borderless** solid accent dot (`.user-location-dot`) with pulse animation to distinguish from bordered waypoint pins.
- **Initial Load:** Start with an empty layer list. On initial load, auto-centers and zooms to user location if no route layers are present.
- **Tile Sizing & Invalidation:** `MapView.tsx` includes `MapResizeHandler` (`ResizeObserver` + delayed `invalidateSize()`) and `<TileLayer keepBuffer={4} />` to prevent blank/unrendered tile strips on mobile viewport changes.
- **Viewport:** Zoom to fit the entire route/geometry within the viewport using `map.fitBounds(target.bounds, { padding: [60, 60] })`.

## Route Planner Conventions
- **Travel Modes:** Order is Cycling → Walking → Driving; **Cycling is the default** profile.
- **Per-stop controls:** Each stop row has a current-location button (`.wp-locate-btn`, `LocateFixed` icon) that fills the stop with the user’s live GPS coords; confirmed stops show an OK indicator + coordinates; the remove button uses the Lucide `X` icon (`.btn-icon-only`).
- **Stop labels:** No visible Start/End/Stop labels — inputs run full-width; the role stays in the waypoint `label` field and is exposed via `aria-label`.
- **Search pick:** Selecting a place suggestion must NOT overwrite the stop’s role `label` (the address lives in the input `query`).
- **Layer naming:** Auto-generated route layer names are plain text with no emoji: `Profile (X.X km, Y min)`, e.g. `Cycling (12.4 km, 45 min)`.

## Route Import Conventions
- **Sources:** `RouteImporter.tsx` defaults to `Komoot link`, with `File upload` as the GPX/GeoJSON fallback. Source toggles reuse `.profile-btn` / `.active` and have no icons.
- **Confirmation:** Both import flows use an icon-free primary button labelled exactly `Import route`; the Komoot loading label is `Importing…`.
- **Komoot links:** Accept Komoot Tour share links and optional `share_token` values. Never request or store Komoot credentials. Validate the hostname/path, discard tracking parameters, and do not log share URLs or tokens.
- **API flow:** The browser posts to `/api/komoot/import`. The server requests GPX first, then falls back on `401` / `403` to public embedded coordinates and generates GPX with the Tour name, coordinates, and available elevation. The browser still uses `parseGPX()` and the shared layer-import callback.
- **Server safety:** Keep upstream Komoot URLs constructed from validated Tour IDs; do not turn the endpoint into a generic URL proxy. Preserve request/response limits, timeouts, and rate limiting.
- **Deployment:** Vite middleware handles local development and preview. Production hosting must support the Node serverless adapter in `api/komoot/import.ts`; a static-only host is insufficient for Komoot imports.
- **Upstream stability:** Komoot's app endpoints are undocumented and can change. Keep their handling isolated in `server/komootImport.ts` and retain manual file upload as a fallback.

## Key Architecture & Files
- `src/App.tsx`: Main app layout, bottom dock, modal management, user location controls, and viewport controllers.
- `src/components/MapView.tsx`: Full-screen Leaflet map, custom waypoint pins, borderless location marker, tile resize handler, and map controllers.
- `src/components/ModalDialog.tsx`: Accessible dialog wrapper with focus trap, aria attributes, and keyboard handling.
- `src/components/LayerCards.tsx`: Floating layer cards with visibility toggle, inline rename, delete, and keyboard activation.
- `src/components/RoutePlanner.tsx`: OSRM routing with driving, walking, and cycling travel profiles.
- `src/components/RouteImporter.tsx`: Komoot/file source selection and shared import callback wiring.
- `src/components/KomootImporter.tsx`: Komoot share-link form, request cancellation, GPX parsing, and import error display.
- `src/components/GeoJSONUploader.tsx`: File importer accepting `.gpx`, `.geojson`, and `.json`.
- `src/components/SearchBox.tsx`: OSM Nominatim place search scoped to current map bounds with keyboard-navigable listbox.
- `src/utils/komoot.ts`: Komoot URL validation, Tour ID extraction, and share-token handling.
- `src/utils/gpx.ts`: Zero-dependency native DOMParser converting GPX tracks/routes/waypoints into GeoJSON with distance and duration calculation.
- `src/utils/waypointMarkers.ts`: Metadata classification and teardrop SVG marker generator with Lucide icons.
- `server/komootImport.ts`: Validated Komoot proxy, GPX retrieval, public-coordinate fallback, and generated GPX response.
- `server/rateLimit.ts`: Best-effort in-memory Komoot import rate limiting.
- `api/komoot/import.ts`: Production serverless adapter for the Komoot import handler.
- `vite.config.ts`: React, HTTPS, and Komoot middleware configuration for development and preview.
- `src/hooks/useMapLayers.ts`: Layer state persisted in `localStorage` with non-overlapping color cycling.
- `src/hooks/useUserLocation.ts`: Live GPS location tracking with permission handling and continuous watching.
- `tests/komoot.test.mjs`: Node tests for URL validation, GPX imports, coordinate fallback, and error handling.

## Validation Commands
- Automated tests: `npm test` (Node test runner; includes Komoot URL, API, fallback, and error-handling coverage)
- Build verification: `npm run build` (`tsc -b && vite build`)
- Dev server: `npm run dev` (running on `https://localhost:5173/` / `https://192.168.x.x:5173/` with local SSL)
- Production preview: `npm run preview` (includes the Komoot middleware after `npm run build`)

